[{"code":"list_may_be_shared","severity":"error","span":{"file":"Main.beni","start":{"line":16,"col":7},"end":{"line":16,"col":18}},"title":"LIST MAY BE SHARED","message":"`[ …old, 2 ]` adds to the end of `old` itself, and the checker cannot show that\nnothing else still holds the list.\n\n15|    fiber = Task.soon λ⊤ → Debug.log \"old ${String.fromInt (List.length old)}\" ⊤\n       ^^^^^ `fiber#Soon.0⋆` keeps the list here\n               ^^^^^^^^^ `fiber#Soon.0⋆` may hold the list through this call\n16|    ( [ …old, 2 ], fiber )\n         ^^^^^^^^^^^ the list is changed in place here\n                      ^^^^^ and `fiber#Soon.0⋆` is read here, after the change\n\nTo be safe, change a copy:\n\n16|    ( [ …List.copy old, 2 ], fiber )\n\nThis is a limit of the checker, not proof of sharing: fiber#Soon.0⋆ may hold it\nthrough the call at 15:13, and is read at 16:5; it was given to JavaScript, or\nkept by a callee."}]
